## How does it work?

Since 2014, Almannarómur has been building a future for Icelandic in technology. We are now launching a new initiative, and we invite Icelandic businesses to take part. The aim is to expand the Icelandic Gigaword Corpus, the core resource behind Icelandic language technology.

{% video src="https://player.vimeo.com/video/1135765344?muted=1&autoplay=1&autopause=0" title="Almannarómur - Þín íslenska er málið" /%}

To take part, register your company or workplace above. As your workplace’s representative, you sign a data transfer agreement online. You can then upload the documents your organization chooses to share.

{% action href="https://almannaromur.is/thin-islenska-er-malid" label="Visit website" /%}

{% band heading="Goal" %}
Almannarómur aims to ensure Icelandic stands on equal footing with other languages in digital development, and that businesses and the public have access to Icelandic language technology. That is how we build a future for Icelandic in technology.
{% /band %}

## How the data is processed

Almannarómur manages the collection, and companies submit their material, such as text documents, through a dedicated upload portal. Examples include reports, procedures, guidelines, memos, presentations, and much more.

The Árni Magnússon Institute then takes over, preparing the data and adding it to the Icelandic Gigaword Corpus.

The Árni Magnússon Institute for Icelandic Studies has handled this kind of data processing for many years. Its role is to ensure the data's quality and usefulness.

1. **Intake and preparation**

   First, the institute standardizes the data and prepares it for processing, aligning file formats and encoding with the corpus’s processing systems. An automatic cleanup then removes unusable characters, HTML code, and passages in other languages.

   What remains at the end of this stage is complete Icelandic text.\
**Please note that this process does not remove sensitive information. Companies must make sure that the material they submit contains nothing confidential.**

2. **Linguistic analysis and segmentation**

   Next, the text goes through automatic linguistic analysis. The analysis:

   - Splits the text into smaller units
   - Tags it with detailed grammatical information
   - Converts it to a consistent data format

   This step is essential. It allows the data to be used in linguistic research and as material for language technology solutions, which work with word forms, sentence structure, and context, among other things.

3. **Publication as an open corpus**

   Once processing is complete, the data becomes part of a dedicated corpus for this project, which the institute publishes under a **Creative Commons BY 4.0** license.

   This makes it open to everyone for research and development, among other uses. The institute splits complete texts into fragments and shuffles them, so **no one can reconstruct the original documents or search them in context**.

   **A shared effort for the future of Icelandic**\
Since 2014, Almannarómur has built the infrastructure for Icelandic language technology in partnership with the Árni Magnússon Institute, universities, and the business sector. This collection drive continues that work. It is an important step toward ensuring Icelandic remains a fully functional language in the digital world. By contributing, companies strengthen the foundation for AI in Icelandic society and help make sure people in Iceland can use modern technology freely, in the Icelandic we speak today.

   More information about the initiative and how to take part is available [here.](https://almannaromur.is/thin-islenska-er-malid)

## Frequently asked questions

{% accordion title="What happens to the data, and how is it processed before it enters the Icelandic Gigaword Corpus?" %}
- The initiative will produce its own corpus, published under the open CC BY 4.0 license (Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International). This means anyone is free to use it.
- You can learn more about the Árni Magnússon Institute’s corpora here: [Íslenski málbankinn](https://malbankinn.is/is/hugvisindi) (the Icelandic language data repository).
{% /accordion %}

{% accordion title="Will sensitive information be removed automatically?" %}
- The cleanup process removes HTML tags, URLs, code, and anything else that is not natural Icelandic text.
- No one reviews the content itself, and the process does not remove anything that could be sensitive. It is therefore especially important that you confirm the documents and data you submit contain no sensitive information of any kind.
{% /accordion %}

{% accordion title="Who will have access to the storage where the data is kept?" %}
Only staff at the Árni Magnússon Institute for Icelandic Studies will have technical access to the submitted data, and only to process it as described above. The purpose is to add the vocabulary and language of Icelandic businesses to our large language collection, improving its quality and diversity.
{% /accordion %}

{% accordion title="Can the documents I submit be reconstructed or searched?" %}
No. When the institute processes texts for a corpus, it splits them into fragments, so any single search returns only limited context.
{% /accordion %}

{% accordion title="Can I ask for my data to be removed from the corpus later?" %}
The Icelandic Gigaword Corpus is updated every year. On request, we can remove your data from future versions, but it will remain in earlier versions. However, we cannot fully withdraw data that is already part of the current or earlier versions.
{% /accordion %}
